msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:23
msgid "Editor"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:27
msgid "Trim the block editor down to what the site uses."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:35
msgid "Don't load patterns from wordpress.org"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:36
msgid "The block editor no longer offers block patterns (ready-made layouts) from the WordPress pattern directory. Patterns from the theme, plugins and your own saved patterns stay available."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:37
msgid "Answers WordPress' should_load_remote_block_patterns filter with no, so the pattern directory is never queried."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:38
msgid "The directory patterns rarely fit the site's design and clutter the inserter. Not loading them also saves requests to wordpress.org."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:39
msgid "Themes that list directory patterns in their theme.json lose those patterns too."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:44
msgid "Turn off block suggestions from wordpress.org"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:45
msgid "When a search in the block inserter finds nothing, the editor no longer offers to install block plugins from the WordPress plugin directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:46
msgid "Removes the block directory script from the block editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:47
msgid "Editors shouldn't install plugins while writing; every installed block is another plugin that has to be maintained and can break."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:52
msgid "Turn off Openverse images"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:53
msgid "Removes the \"Openverse\" tab from the media section of the block inserter, which searches free images on openverse.org."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:54
msgid "Sets the block editor setting enableOpenverseMediaCategory to false."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:55
msgid "Openverse images come with licence conditions (often attribution) that editors easily overlook, and the search sends requests to openverse.org."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:70
msgid "Use the classic editor for"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:71
msgid "Content of the selected types opens in the classic editor instead of the block editor. Pages built with Elementor are not affected: they open in Elementor either way."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:72
msgid "Answers WordPress' use_block_editor_for_post_type filter with no for the selected types. If another plugin already turned the block editor off for a type, it stays off."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:73
msgid "Some content (e.g. simple entries of a custom post type) is easier to edit in the classic editor, and some plugins expect it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Editor/EditorModule.php:74
msgid "Content already made with blocks is shown as HTML in the classic editor; editing it there can break the blocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Elementor/ElementorModule.php:25
msgid "Elementor"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Elementor/ElementorModule.php:29
msgid "Settings for sites built with Elementor. Only shown while Elementor is active."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Elementor/ElementorModule.php:37
msgid "Open Elementor pages in Elementor"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Elementor/ElementorModule.php:38
msgid "For content built with Elementor, the title in the page and post lists and \"Edit\" in the toolbar open Elementor directly. In the lists, the duplicate \"Edit with Elementor\" link is replaced by a \"WordPress editor\" link. Content not built with Elementor keeps opening in the WordPress editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Elementor/ElementorModule.php:39
msgid "Checks Elementor's own marker that a post was built with it and, only on the post list screens and for the toolbar's \"Edit\" link, points the edit link to Elementor's editor. Other edit links (e.g. redirects after saving) are not changed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Elementor/ElementorModule.php:40
msgid "Editors of Elementor sites almost always want Elementor. Opening the WordPress editor first is an extra click and confusing, because the page content isn't editable there."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Elementor/ElementorModule.php:83
msgid "WordPress editor"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:38
msgid "Environment"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:42
msgid "Tell live, staging and development copies of the site apart. WordPress knows which one it is from the WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE setting in wp-config.php (many hosts set it for staging sites automatically); without it, every site counts as live."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:50
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:51
msgid "Only on staging, development and local sites"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:52
msgid "On every site, including the live one"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:55
msgid "Environment badge in the toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:56
msgid "Shows a coloured label in the toolbar: \"Live\" (red), \"Staging\" (yellow), \"Development\" (blue) or \"Local\" (green)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:57
msgid "Adds a toolbar item with the environment WordPress reports (from WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE) and colours it with a small inline style, in the admin and on the website."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:58
msgid "With the live site and a staging copy open side by side, it's easy to change the wrong one. The badge makes it obvious at a glance."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:63
msgid "Keep non-live sites out of search engines"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:64
msgid "On staging, development and local sites, every page tells search engines not to index it or follow its links, regardless of the \"Search engine visibility\" setting. The live site is never affected."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:65
msgid "Sets the robots meta tag to \"noindex, nofollow\" (also the one Yoast SEO prints) and sends the same as an X-Robots-Tag HTTP header, only when WordPress' environment type is not \"production\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:66
msgid "Staging copies that end up in Google compete with the real site (duplicate content) and show unfinished pages to customers. The WordPress setting is easily forgotten when copying a site back and forth."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:71
msgid "Send as usual"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:72
msgid "Don't send any emails"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:72
msgid "Every email is stopped; forms and shops still report success."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:73
msgid "Send all emails to the address below instead"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:73
msgid "Every email goes only to that address, with the original recipients in the subject."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:76
msgid "Emails on non-live sites"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:77
msgid "What happens to emails sent by staging, development and local sites: form notifications, orders, password resets, Wordfence alerts and so on. The live site is never affected."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:78
msgid "\"Don't send\" stops every email before it is sent and reports it as sent. \"Send to\" replaces all recipients with the address below, removes CC and BCC, and adds the original recipients to the subject, e.g. \"[Staging] New order (to: customer@example.com)\". Both apply only when WordPress' environment type is not \"production\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:79
msgid "A staging copy contains real customers and form recipients. Without this, testing a form on staging sends real emails to real people."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:80
msgid "Blocked emails are reported as sent, so forms don't show errors. Mail plugins that replace WordPress' mail function entirely are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:85
msgid "Redirect emails to"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Environment/EnvironmentModule.php:86
msgid "The address that receives all emails when \"Send all emails to the address below\" is chosen."
msgstr ""

